    "special": "splice",
    "min_len": 80,
    "max_len": 105,
    "comment": "Translated from the singly spliced SP1 RNA, not from the genome as laid down. Soussan 2000 (PMID 10619861, J Clin Invest 105:55-60) states the product verbatim: 'This protein, with 93 amino acids, begins at the polymerase start codon and includes the first 46 amino acids of the polymerase, followed by the 47 amino acids corresponding to a new HBV amino acid sequence generated by the frameshift.' That paper gives no nucleotide coordinates and names no reference genome, and the 2447/489 pair quoted by secondary sources is in EcoRI numbering: applied to NC_003977.2 it lands on AT and CC, not GT and AG. The junction here was therefore located on NC_003977.2 by splice chemistry and confirmed against the paper's own description -- donor 2449 (GT), acceptor 545 (AG), giving join(2309..2449,545..685), 93 aa partitioned exactly 46 + 47, with the first 46 byte-identical to the unspliced polymerase N-terminus. The +2 against the quoted 2447 is the EcoRI offset, the same one that puts HM153811 P at 2307 where this genome has 2309. The reference in Splice-Variants spans the origin, which only works because the contig is still doubled at this stage of the pipe. NOTE: the four deposits in this dump annotated 'spliced protein' are 111 aa, not 93, so they are a different splice product and are deliberately not this feature.",
